From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radium Wang <249038647+radium-wang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:19:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: render Switch HD rumble through DualSense USB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Core Haptics folds each grip’s two bands into intensity and sharpness. Send the timed bands as 48 kHz USB waveforms to the left and right grips when one DualSense is unambiguously connected as player 1. Keep the regular haptics route when USB output is unavailable.

Double the base USB synthesis gain and apply the existing strength slider on top, with a per-grip peak limit. Exercise the signal path, strength, cutoff, and reset in t_haptics_apple.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1993
Reason: Carry Mac DualSense USB HD rumble while the upstream pull request is open.
Issue: seedds/nxnative#1993

